+/**
+ * Process-wide singleton "owner" wrapper around pimShortcutLoop, the install
+ * step that creates/removes Windows .lnk shortcuts. One of 7 near-identical
+ * Loop-owner wrapper singletons in pim_core.
+ *
+ * Locking contract: TryLock()-gated on an internal mutex, held for the full
+ * duration of the operation (released by Status() on completion, or by
+ * Kill()) -- same pattern as pimCopier/pimRegEdit/pimServices/pimDownloader.
+ *
+ * Confirmed gap: Cancel() only sets a flag; it does NOT call anything on the
+ * owned pimShortcutLoop, so a cancelled shortcut operation keeps running to
+ * natural completion. The confirmed caller (pimEntitlement) compensates by
+ * polling for a grace period after Cancel() and calling Kill() if the
+ * operation has not finished by then.
+ *
+ * Also confirmed: Status()'s percent_done output parameter is declared but
+ * never written anywhere in the implementation -- do not build a progress
+ * UI around it without reading pimShortcutLoop state directly instead.
+ *
+ * Sole caller in this codebase: pimEntitlement.
+ */
 class pimShortcuts
 {
 private:
